          "text": "CLINICAL INDICATION  \nRoutine EEG for evaluation of clinically established drug-resistant focal epilepsy with focal-to-bilateral tonic-clonic seizures. Seizure onset occurred at age 9 years, with a current frequency of approximately one seizure per month. Etiology is genetic, associated with a causative PCDH19 variant, c.918G>A. Current antiseizure medications are brivaracetam and lamotrigine.\n\nTECHNIQUE  \nRoutine EEG recording. Further technical and acquisition details were not provided.\n\nFINDINGS  \nNo EEG background, interictal, or ictal findings were provided for interpretation.\n\nIMPRESSION  \nNo electrographic interpretation can be rendered from the available information. The clinical history is of drug-resistant focal epilepsy with focal-to-bilateral tonic-clonic seizures in the setting of a causative PCDH19 c.918G>A variant.",
